                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital admission of your 81-year-old female patient from 17th to 18th July 2016. She was admitted due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, clinical examination revealed reduced breath sounds, prolonged expiration, and significant dyspnoea. Chest X-ray confirmed pulmonary hyperinflation without pneumonic infiltrates. Blood tests and arterial blood gas analysis showed mild hypoxaemia with compensated respiratory acidosis. Pulse oximetry monitoring was maintained throughout her stay. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. The patient received education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management. She is discharged in stable condition and I kindly recommend close follow-up and continued optimisation of her inhaler regimen. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>
               </text>
